# The place the server picks when it is told none and can make none: TMPDIR
# names a directory no machine has, PASLS_SCRATCH is unset, and
# `TemporaryDirectory` fails (ADR-0363). What stood here as a fallback would
# have composed `pasls-<pid>.pas` at the top of TMPDIR -- the guessable name
# the private directory exists to stop -- so the fallback is instead a path
# nothing can create, and this session pins that the server then behaves as
# it does for an unwritable PASLS_SCRATCH: says so once per document, names
# the path, publishes nothing, answers an empty outline, shuts down cleanly.
#
# The conversation is `unwritable`'s, word for word: the two are one behaviour
# reached by two roads, and a session that differed would be pinning a
# difference that is not there.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"processId":null,"rootUri":null,"capabilities":{}}}

# No publishDiagnostics follows: there is nothing to say and saying an empty
# set would claim the file is clean.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didOpen","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas","languageId":"pascal","version":1,"text":"program hello(output);\nbegin\n  writeln('hello')\nend.\n"}}}

# And the outline is empty rather than absent, which is what a client that
# asked for one has to be given.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"textDocument/documentSymbol","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas"}}}

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didClose","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas"}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"shutdown"}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"exit"}
